<title>USA: Norfolk Southern Corp Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Norfolk Southern Corp Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>($ millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					   First Quarter     Pct Change</p>
<p>								    Favorable</p>
<p>					1997	  1996  (Unfavorable)</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		 1,249.7    1,215.0	   3%</p>
<p> Operating Expenses		   964.1	954.0	 (1%)</p>
<p> Income from Operations	     285.6	261.0	   9%</p>
<p> Nonoperating Income (Expense)    (9.9)	  5.8	   --</p>
<p> Net Income			     177.5	168.1	   6%</p>
<p> Earnings per Share		    1.42	 1.31	   8%</p>
<p> Railway Operating Ratio (%)	 73.1	 74.2</p>
<p>NOTES: 1997 nonoperating expense excludes a one-time charge of $77.2 million, $49.7 million after-tax, or $0.40/shr, for costs incurred to establish and maintain a $13 billion credit facility to acquire all of Conrail. As a result of the agreement with CSX concerning the division of Conrail, all but $1.65 billion of that facility has been terminated.</p>
<p>	  Including the credit facility charge, net income was</p>
<p>$127.8 million, 24 percent below 1996, and earnings per share were $1.02, 22 percent below 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
